Local CDATA fragment cases for GATE-03. Upstream (html5lib-tests @
9329e646) covers CDATA sections in foreign document content (tests21.dat)
but has no foreign-fragment records with CDATA; these pin the tokenizer's
adjusted-current-node gate through the context-aware fragment parser: SVG,
MathML, and MathML text integration point contexts accept the section, an
HTML context does not, an HTML integration point inside foreign content
still does (the gate is the current node's namespace), and only "]]>" ends
the section.
#data
<![CDATA[<b>&amp;]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| "<b>&amp;"

#data
<![CDATA[foo]]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| "foo]"

#data
<![CDATA[]] >]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
math math
#document
| "]] >"

#data
<![CDATA[foo]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
div
#document
| <!-- [CDATA[foo]] -->

#data
<svg><![CDATA[foo]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| <svg svg>
|   "foo"

#data
<svg><foreignObject><![CDATA[foo]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| <svg svg>
|   <svg foreignObject>
|     "foo"

#data
<svg><foreignObject><div><![CDATA[foo]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| <svg svg>
|   <svg foreignObject>
|     <div>
|       <!-- [CDATA[foo]] -->

#data
<![CDATA[foo
#errors
#document-fragment
svg svg
#document
| "foo"

#data
<![CDATA[foo]]>
#errors
#document-fragment
math mi
#document
| "foo"
